# -*- mode: python ; coding: utf-8 -*-
"""WARPRAND-APP-001 - the standalone Windows build of the warp randomizer.

Same shape as ``DragonByte Z.spec``, deliberately: a **onedir** ``COLLECT``
build rather than a one-file archive. The ticket allows either, and one-file is
rejected here on measured grounds - PySide6 unpacks its Qt libraries to a
temporary directory on every launch, which costs seconds of startup and is the
mode most likely to be quarantined by an anti-virus heuristic. One directory
extracted from a zip starts in the time a normal application does.

The single data file is the ROM profile catalog. ``webfoot.cli.load_catalog``
prefers a checkout's ``config/roms.yaml`` and otherwise falls back to
``tools.webfoot.data/roms.yaml``, which is the branch a frozen build takes - so
that file must travel or every ROM selection is refused.

Nothing from the commercial ROM is bundled, and nothing can be: the profile
catalog is a table of addresses and hashes, not game content.

Trimmed payload
---------------

PySide6's PyInstaller hook collects the whole Qt SDK, so a QtWidgets-only
application otherwise ships QtQml, QtQuick, QtPdf, QtVirtualKeyboard and every
Qt translation - about 35 MB of libraries that are never loaded by a single
window with three text fields, a button and a progress bar. Dropping them takes
the release from ~45 MB to ~20 MB.

Two things are deliberately NOT dropped:

* ``opengl32sw.dll``, the software OpenGL fallback. It is the largest remaining
  binary and it is kept on purpose: it is what makes the window render on a
  machine with no usable GL driver, and the ticket puts reliability above size.
* ``Qt6Network`` and the TLS plugins, which Qt's platform layer may reach for
  through QDesktopServices ("Open Folder").

The exclusions are asserted by the packaged smoke run, which drives the real
frozen executable.
"""

#: Python modules nothing here imports.
_UNUSED_QT_MODULES = [
    'PySide6.QtQml',
    'PySide6.QtQuick',
    'PySide6.QtQuickWidgets',
    'PySide6.QtPdf',
    'PySide6.QtPdfWidgets',
    'PySide6.QtVirtualKeyboard',
]

#: Native libraries and data belonging to those modules, matched on their
#: bundle-relative path with forward slashes.
_UNUSED_QT_PREFIXES = (
    'PySide6/Qt6Qml',
    'PySide6/Qt6Quick',
    'PySide6/Qt6Pdf',
    'PySide6/Qt6VirtualKeyboard',
    'PySide6/translations/',
)


def _is_unused_qt(relative: str) -> bool:
    normalised = relative.replace('\\', '/')
    return normalised.startswith(_UNUSED_QT_PREFIXES)


a = Analysis(
    ['tools/webfoot/warprand/_pyinstaller_entry.py'],
    pathex=['.'],
    binaries=[],
    datas=[('tools/webfoot/data/roms.yaml', 'tools/webfoot/data')],
    hiddenimports=[],
    hookspath=[],
    hooksconfig={},
    runtime_hooks=[],
    excludes=_UNUSED_QT_MODULES,
    noarchive=False,
    optimize=0,
)

a.binaries = [item for item in a.binaries if not _is_unused_qt(item[0])]
a.datas = [item for item in a.datas if not _is_unused_qt(item[0])]

pyz = PYZ(a.pure)

exe = EXE(
    pyz,
    a.scripts,
    [],
    exclude_binaries=True,
    name='Buu-Fury-Warp-Randomizer',
    debug=False,
    bootloader_ignore_signals=False,
    strip=False,
    upx=True,
    console=False,
    disable_windowed_traceback=False,
    argv_emulation=False,
    target_arch=None,
    codesign_identity=None,
    entitlements_file=None,
)
coll = COLLECT(
    exe,
    a.binaries,
    a.datas,
    strip=False,
    upx=True,
    upx_exclude=[],
    name='Buu-Fury-Warp-Randomizer',
)
